From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 15:57:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] clk: samsung: clk-cpu: add Exynos7870 CPU clock layout

For CPU DVFS purposes the Exynos7870 behaves like an Exynos850: there
is no armclk divider inside CMU_CPUCLx (the cores are fed straight from
the CLK_CPUCLx mux) and the alternate parent speed is adjusted through
the CLKCMU_CPUCLx_SWITCH divider, which sits in CMU_MIF on this SoC.
That gives the 800/400/266/200 MHz park rates the vendor DFS driver
uses.

The register format however predates the Exynos850: the mux select is
on bit 12, with a separate MUX_STAT register 0x400 above the mux whose
field [13:12] reads sel+1 once stable, and none of the existing layouts
can drive it (the Exynos5433 one would write its divider values into
what are status registers here).

Add CPUCLK_LAYOUT_E7870: Exynos850-style pre/post rate handlers with
the Exynos7870 mux and status accessors, no divider programming (no
divider on the CPU path depends on the level), and an alternate parent
helper with one extra parent hop for the gate at the CMU_MIF boundary.

Register cluster0_clk and cluster1_clk with the 13 levels usable on
this SoC, 1586000 down to 342875 kHz: 2002 and 1924 MHz are disabled in
the ECT DVFS block, and 1794 and 1690 MHz have no valid voltage in the
fused ASV table.  The pre-rate handler rejects any rate that is not
listed, so this table is what keeps the CPUs off those levels.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
---

Notes:
    Origin: https://github.com/alessandro-fontana/linux-exynos7870 commit f2072e926937 (branch gtaxlwifi/7.3). Port to v7.3.4: applied unchanged (git am, no fuzz).

 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-cpu.c        | 164 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-cpu.h        |   2 +
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos7870.c |  45 ++++++++
